@startuml

title NETWORK_ID_SPOOFING1 - Adversarial Commit Attempt

== Initialization Phase ==
autonumber “<b>(I##)”
box "Program Maintainer" #LightGreen
actor "R3 Maintainer" as R3
end box

box "Attacker / Malicious Network Operator" #pink
actor "Malicious Notary" as MN
end box

box "Solana Cluster" #lightblue
participant "Solana Notary Program" as SNP
database "Solana Cluster (PDA Storage)" as SC
end box

note over R3,SNP
Program deployment by R3 (out of band for DF_* flow).
end note
R3 -> SNP: <color brown>**DF_STN_INIT_PROGRAM**</color> \n Initialize program, R3 becomes admin

note over R3,SNP
R3 creates Network A (network_id=0) and authorizes a legitimate notary.
end note
note over MN,SNP
Malicious operator registers Network B (network_id=1).
end note

note over MN
Attacker is a valid notary for Network A (network_id=0).
They attempt to spoof Network B (network_id=1).
end note

== Adversarial Commit Phase ==
autonumber “<b>(S##)”

MN -> MN: <color green>**Forge Commit Instruction**</color> \n Build tx_id + inputs
MN -> MN: <color green>**Sign Transaction**</color> \n Sign with notary key
MN -> MN: <color green>**Spoof Accounts**</color> \n Provide output PDA derived with network_id=1
MN -> SNP: <color green>**DF_STN_INVOKE_COMMIT**</color> \n Invoke commit with spoofed PDA

SNP -> SNP: <color green>**DF_STN_VERIFY_ACCOUNT_COUNT**</color> \n Verify accounts list
SNP -> SC: <color green>**DF_STN_CHECK_PDA_EXISTENCE**</color> \n Load NotaryAuthorization (network_id=0)
SNP -> SNP: Re-derive expected output PDA with network_id=0

alt PDA mismatch detected
    SNP -> SNP: <color brown>**InvalidAccounts**</color> \n Output PDA != expected PDA
    SNP -> MN: <color brown>**DF_STN_RETURN_FAILURE**</color> \n Reject spoofed commit
else PDA matches
    SNP -> SC: <color green>**DF_STN_CREATE_OUTPUT_ACCOUNT**</color> \n Create/initialize output account
    SNP -> MN: <color green>**DF_STN_RETURN_SUCCESS**</color> \n Commit succeeds
end

@enduml
